WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.220
So I've been in touch over the last couple
of weeks with some of our viewers in Hong

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.891
Kong and one in particular has [inaudible].

00:00:05.891 --> 00:00:10.400
You've been sending me videos, videos that
have been taken by others, some posted on

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.600
social media from Hong Kong, some taken by
the viewers, family themselves.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.210
And I have a video for you today that that
is utterly insane in a despicable sight to

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.210
behold.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:28.789
And the video is of what appear to be police
on motorcycles running over protesters at

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:30.070
high speed.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:37.200
This is not, you know, someone's toe caught
under a motorcycle tire in a confusing moment

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.550
accidentally or something like that.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:45.310
This is police or what appear to be police
revving up and accelerating at high speed

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.950
and hitting protestors.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:51.210
Of course, viewer discretion is advised, all
of that stuff.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.690
I know this is very visual, so if you're merely
listening to the podcast or on the radio today,

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.720
you won't get the full scope.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.630
But indulge me for the 28 seconds that we're
about to watch.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:19.360
And then I encourage you to find the video
on our YouTube channel.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:33.909
[inaudible]

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:37.220
absolutely and utterly insane.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.820
And things in Hong Kong just don't appear
to be slowing down at all.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.870
In fact, violence may be getting worse.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:48.509
Lawmakers, uh, who are activating for democracy
have been facing arrest.

00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:54.310
Police have been using more and more a tear
gas protestors are blocking main roads, cars

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.479
are being lit on fire.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:58.950
A man was actually set on fire a couple of
days ago.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.799
We heard from a Hong Kong, uh, police senior
superintendent who said quote, over the past

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:11.120
two days, our society has been pushed to the
brink of a total breakdown that can be interpreted

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.500
in at least two or three different ways depending
on which side of the protests you find yourself

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.500
on.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.390
Here's video of people being pepper sprayed
or teargassed at close range.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.980
This video is reminiscent of that.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:28.700
Remember that CIC police officer, I think
his name was Lieutenant pike, John pike, I

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.570
believe at UC Berkeley some years ago.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:35.810
Just at point blank range, uh, spraying almost
like you would with, with sunscreen.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.310
Spang spraying protesters, uh, with tear gas.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:52.620
This is video from Bloomberg in Hong Kong.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:03:03.730
[inaudible].

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.680
So right now, this is, this is just horrible
stuff.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:12.370
A district council elections are set for November
24 but the longer that this goes, the more

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:18.840
people are fearing China could get involved
and pressure Hong Kong to postpone those elections.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:25.030
Even to go around Hong Kong's legislature
all together to pass national security legislation

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:28.960
as they're calling it police shooting at protestor.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.070
That video went viral.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.070
The man set on fire.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.570
I told you about that video going viral.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.530
The man was arguing with protesters.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.260
He was some kind of flammable liquid, I don't
know if it was alcohol or or, or a gasoline

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.060
thrown on him and then lit on fire.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.230
We have those videos.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.970
I'm not going to play them right now, but
you can easily find them online if you're

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.040
so inclined.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.070
I genuinely have no idea how this will settle.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.870
It's getting uglier and uglier.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:04:00.310
Uh, I would say by the day, certainly by the
week and no sign whatsoever of a deescalation

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.310
anytime soon.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.200
So that's my question to you.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:11.150
If you think ahead a week, a month, six months,
however long, what do you see as even having

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.860
the potential to deescalate circumstances?

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.860
I don't know the answer.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.860
I want to hear from you.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:22.340
Leave a reply if you're watching on YouTube
or send me a tweet at D Pacman, if you are

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.830
watching or listening elsewhere.

